==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]].
*Infinite [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Loris]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*2 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Master A.]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
**1 [[Mr. Mole]] spawns.
**1 [[Loris]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This level introduces Surge Base, which is like [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]], but makes a  level 3 surge attack with a fast frequency instead of a wave attack with a long attack frequency. The surge will spawn in a random location inside its wide attack range, which is 2000. Due to Surge Base's inescapable RNG combined with its ridiculous attack power, its recommended to bring any Surge Immune attackers, such as  Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon]], [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi: N2]] or any surge immune ubers.

At the start of the level, stall out the Loris for full cash. Once that's done, hit the base, lure the Loris that spawn on base hit, and kill it quickly, using Idi. From here, use Idi, [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] carefully to chip down the Mr. Mole and Master A. If you happen to own [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]], he helps immensely in this stage due to his extremely high damage against Traitless enemies.

On future clears of this stage, having high base HP is necessary due to Mr. Mole gaining dangerous damage per hit. Alone, both Traitless bosses are easily repelled using crowd-controllers such as [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]], [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] and the Breakerblast cannon, so you can focus on killing the Celeboodle and Sir Rels.

